    "facingRegistration": "102234f0 property metadata; 10d4f5a0 places yaw at11254ea8 and pitch at11254eb0; 1021e8c0 converts authored degrees with float pi/180 at10d93e54.",
    "targetReferences": "Both evaluators resolve current actor handle and 103b8af0 target handle, fail on missing/stale generation, and subtract actor GameObject matrix translation from target translation. No muzzle/skin offset in these two conditions.",
    "worldForward": "101e5ee0..101e5f18 negates actor matrix rowZ at +24,+28,+2c (matrix begins transform+4).",
    "yaw": "101e5f6d..101e5f79 zeroes both forward.y and targetDelta.y, then normalizes both. acos(clamped dot) at101e5fb5..101e6021.",
    "pitch": "101e5f80 normalizes forward;101e5f8b normalizes targetDelta;101e5f90..101e5fa2 replaces targetDelta.xz with normalized forward.xz;101e5fae normalizes altered target vector; then acos(clamped dot). Signed=false bypasses101e602b..101e6070 sign logic.",
    "pitchConsequence": "For horizontal normalized forward, pitch=atan(abs(delta.y)/length(delta)), not atan2(abs(delta.y),horizontalLength(delta)). Raw30deg boundary corresponds to a geometric elevation about35.264deg. Raw40deg corresponds about57.045deg. Actual body pitch changes this formula; source is not reduced to a fixed elevation threshold.",
    "normalize": "107badf0 normalizes in place; squared length below float9.999999439624929e-11 becomes zero. No hypothetical vector algorithm inferred from field name.",
    "distance": "1011e6de..1011e728 builds target-minus-actor translation,107bc530 dots it with actor matrix rows (no second translation).107de5a0 switch:0X,1Y,2Z,3XZ length,4XYZ length,5AbsX,6AbsY,7AbsZ.",
    "comparisons": "1009e110 direct floating compare implements strict/non-strict source comparator; uses native floats. Java uses double Vec3/Math, preserving formula and operator rather than claiming bit-identical native roundoff."
  },
