  "implementation": [
    "HelicopterTactics selects profile from verified Spawn BranchRefs, not string-name similarity. HOVER/NONE have no gun envelope.",
    "HelicopterCombat.fire applies only to AI !rocket, after current crew/phase/hostility/rotor checks and before effects. It uses current target root hull position when enemy rides a military vehicle/aircraft; actual ray still targets the observed skin/part point.",
    "Distance adapter uses1MCblock/sourceUnit, already chosen for live helicopter navigation; preserves actor-local XZ and Y. Source gun envelope is separate from current MC muzzle3D range8..72: both must pass. The100-source-unit strafe maximum does not extend the existing72-block physical shot range; source1-unit minimum does not remove8-block muzzle safety.",
    "MC body basis uses HelicopterArmament.rotate yaw+bank and authored+Z forward. Source -matrixRowZ is mapped to+Z; XZ distance is invariant to the forward sign. Native full aircraft transform/scale is not asserted reproduced.",
    "No player manualFire/rapid, guided missile/hover, targeting permissions, wall/friendly first obstruction, ammo stores, sync fields, protocol, placement, destruction or assets are changed.",
    "Lost observation already releases active tactics/airspace, aborts Hellfire and suppresses firing via seen gate. Removed/invalid target clears target state; persistent occlusion exits combat after100 missed updates. No duplicate loss policy added.",
    "Source simple rocket branch140 contains False97472. This change does not invent random gun/rocket selection from a branch label or disturb existing verified hover Hellfire lifecycle."
  ],
  "remaining": [
    "Full gun branch timer/aim episode lifecycles are outside this gate change; existing 80/80-tick MC gun cycle remains, so no claim of complete branch151 timer reproduction.",
    "TargetHasLoF source cached radius0.2/offset1 query and damage-class-specific gun profiles are not implemented by this helper; current actual loaded muzzle/first-obstruction checks remain.",
    "Native aircraft transform scale/pitch is not recreated; MC uses its existing unit yaw+bank basis and positiveZ model forward. Distances follow existing navigation adapter one block/source unit."
  ],
